<title>GERMANY: Veba, RWE dive on C&amp;W report.</title>
<headline>Veba, RWE dive on C&amp;W report.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in German diversified utilities Veba AG and RWE AG fell heavily in pre-bourse trade on Monday following a British newspaper report that Cable &amp; Wireless Plc was planning to exit its telecom alliance with them.</p>
<p>The Times earlier on Monday reported that the British group was looking to abandon its alliance with Veba and RWE. Veba fell 1.89 marks to 88.46, while RWE shares slipped 1.10 marks to 67.80.</p>
<p>Dealers said the report had prompted some profit-taking in the German utility sector that had recently been setting in after a strong bull run in the sector.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
